WEBVTT

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.690
Come on, Deidara!

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.070
Let's stop messing around and go already!

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:38.950
I'm not messing around.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:43.040
Look this delicate yet bold creation.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.110
It's almost too artistic. Hmm.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.530
But it's just gonna explode, right?

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.580
You dunce!

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.600
Destruction is eternal beauty.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.880
In other words, art—

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.270
Did I just peek into eternity?

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:01.720
No!

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.140
This piece of garbage...

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.560
<b>Leaf Diary</b>

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.560
<b>I will defend the 
Leaf from disaster!</b>

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.420
Actually, this could prove 
to be interesting, hmm.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.990
<b>Autumn Shinobi Safety Lessons!</b>

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.160
Lady Tsunade,

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.320
lately there's been an increase 
in ninjutsu accidents...

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.420
...caused by neglect and carelessness.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.250
I'll need to think of a way to address this.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.880
Why don't we start a safety 
awareness campaign?

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.410
You think that'd be enough 
to change anything?

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.800
And on top of that,

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.620
a performance where we...

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.020
Psst psst psst.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.710
Hmm...

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.780
We didn't have to disguise ourselves
and come all the way to the Leaf.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.180
To us, the Leaf Village 
is one giant eyesore.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.310
Laying a few threats down on 
them fits with our agenda.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.920
You're sure it's not because you
have a grudge against them?

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.100
Say hello to Deidara and Tobi.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.730
Members of Akatsuki, 
the evil organization...

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.760
...bent on terrorizing the world.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:19.670
Get the lead out!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.450
What's that light?

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.930
Hey, what're you doing?!

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:28.560
Move it!

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.980
Stop!

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.270
What was that for?!

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.110
I think you already know.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.050
<i>No way. Did they figure out who I am?</i>

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.240
You were going ten kilometers 
over the speed limit!

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:47.940
What?!

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.160
Don't play dumb.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.160
My eyes can't be tricked!

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.120
Wow, the Byakugan can detect speed?

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.670
What is this?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.550
You're so oblivious! How could 
you fall for a speed trap?

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.970
That other guy even flashed 
his lights to warn us!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.500
You should've stopped me!

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.040
Wait, what?

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:11.720
When a passing car flashes his lights,

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.440
he's warning you there's a cop ahead.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.310
<b>Speed 
Limit</b>

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.850
<i>Stare...</i>

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.130
But it's rare that anyone 
gets stopped around here

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:24.530
<b>Speed 
Limit
Strictly 
Enforced</b>

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.370
We've had a lot of reckless 
ninjutsu drivers out here lately,

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.530
so we're cracking down hard.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.190
What on earth is a 
reckless ninjutsu driver?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.060
Are people sleepwalking, 
or blocking mountain passes...

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.140
on the weekends or something?

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.730
We appreciate your cooperation.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:36.690
May we see your license, please?

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:37.460
<i>L-Lic...</i>

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.090
<i>License?</i>

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.800
Hurry up, or they'll get suspicious!

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.870
Don't tell me you don't have one.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:47.220
Er, I, uh...

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.890
Looks like I'll have to handle this.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.310
Juggling?

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.980
That's amazing!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.520
I'm a 3rd degree ninja performer!

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:05.320
Six Paths Ninjutsu 
Performance Academy
3rd Degree - Sir Tobi

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.580
This is my certificate.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:05.320
This actually exists?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.500
I'm also a 2nd degree 
space-time ninjutsu user,

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:09.980
a promoter for Make-Out Tactics,

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.680
and a military sommelier.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.120
You're quite a go-getter.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.840
In today's economy,

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.520
it's helpful to have lots of qualifications.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.500
Hey, hold it!

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.040
Those aren't even close 
to being drivers' licenses.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.810
Oh please, this was never 
about drivers' licenses.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:25.420
Precisely.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.300
This is a driving test 
designed to measure...

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.720
...your techniques to weasel 
your way out of a ticket.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:35.320
There wasn't any real technique
involved, other than smooth talking.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.460
Byakugan!

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.330
Next you'll need to take a sobriety test.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.890
<i>At least this one seems straightforward.</i>

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:46.900
<i>They're just checking to see 
if I've been drinking alcohol, hmm.</i>

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.810
Please blow in here.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.080
Fine.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.780
Please don't interrupt!

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.830
There's no need for that.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.130
My compatriot here would 
never turn to the bottle.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.310
He's a true artist!

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:01.630
Tobi, are you...

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.760
I truly love his art.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:07.930
It's not just raw strength, 
it's got real impact!

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:08.990
And, also—

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:10.720
Yes, yes, exactly.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.790
It's a select few ninjas who can

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:16.350
elevate ninjutsu to the 
level of true art. Hmm.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.890
Deidara, you're so cool!

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.400
All things with form are 
destined to crumble.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:28.860
But a violent explosion burns itself
into the memory for all eternity!

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.820
It's the ultimate art—

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.580
Nope, you fail.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:36.130
Way over the legal limit.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:38.820
You're completely drunk 
off your own talent.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.330
He's drunk?

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.380
He's always like this.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.250
Mmhmm.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.170
Who's side are you on?!

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.840
What's the point of all this?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.350
Being drunk makes you weave all
over the road like a wild snake.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.270
Like Orochimaru!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:03.690
You don't have to work that traitor
in just because you said "snake!"

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:10.340
Enough of this. Let us 
in the village already!

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:12.620
We've tested them pretty thoroughly.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.360
They're good, right, Lee?

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:15.660
I'm afraid not.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.270
There's more?

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.820
One last check.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:21.220
Something you absolutely 
cannot be without.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.330
What?

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.590
Brakes!

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.940
<i>More of this nonsense?</i>

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:33.510
Deidara, leave this part to me.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:39.440
<i>I'm just your everyday,
ordinary office lady.</i>

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:42.620
<i>Totally average. Nothing special about me.</i>

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:45.720
<i>Well, maybe one thing where
no one else can best me.</i>

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:47.570
<i>And that's my undying 
admiration for Mr. Daraday.</i>

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.490
<i>My love...</i>

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.940
Oh, come off it.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:08:01.430
A homely dame like Tobiko's 
not even on my radar!

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.450
What's the matter?

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:10.040
What's got a strong-willed girl 
like you crying her eyes out?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.840
I've made my choice.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.680
The works!

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.980
I will be pretty!

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.150
I didn't even recognize you, Tobiko!

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:39.140
Are you going to get him to ask you out,

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:41.790
or take the initiative yourself?

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.920
It doesn't matter, Zetsy.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.280
But you've always wanted Mr. Daraday—

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.340
Yes, but...

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:53.150
Mr. Daraday's... just a playboy.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.430
He stepped on the brakes?!

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.060
Spectacular braking!

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:06.600
You can stop yourself 
when things get risky!

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.400
That's a vital ability for a shinobi to have—

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.110
I don't think that's true!

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.720
Now it's your turn.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.360
Let's see it!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.530
M-Me?

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.620
Brakes, huh?

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.960
The rules are simple.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:27.420
Step on it, and stop as close to the
edge of the cliff as you can.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.690
I'm no chicken either, Dean!

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.590
Let's rumble, Toby!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:33.940
Go!

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.050
Any closer and I'll...

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.620
He didn't even touch the brakes!

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:05.030
Anyone scared enough to hit the brakes

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.790
will never be a true artist! Hmm.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.640
What's the meaning of this?!

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:10.730
Quiet!

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:15.140
Delay us any more and I'll blow the
lot of you to kingdom come!

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:17.470
Uh oh, he snapped.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.970
This guy seems really dangerous.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.010
That thing's got a ton of 
chakra crammed into it.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:24.080
It could blow at any time.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.140
Blow...

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.680
Wait, are you—

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:30.980
Lee, we've got big trouble!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:34.160
It's time for the show and 
the actors haven't arrived!

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.470
Don't worry.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.370
Hurry everyone!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:43.560
<b>Autumn Safety Presentation</b>

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:44.990
We're starting a bit late, 
but please enjoy the show!

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:50.090
I think they mistook us for the actors.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.290
I should be thanking them.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.680
We're gonna give 'em a sample 
of one of my creations.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.800
Art...

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.220
...is a blast!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.590
You fools!

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.010
As you can see,

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:08.080
if I catch anyone doing something 
unsafe, like reckless ninjutsu driving,

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.710
I'll beat the daylights outta them.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:10.540
That is all!

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:15.310
I bet the stage show really drove
home the dangers of reckless driving,

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:17.640
and made everyone more safety conscious.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:22.250
I think it drove home the danger 
of Lady Tsunade more...

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:24.780
Regardless, we should 
far fewer accidents now.

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.630
And those two actors...

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:29.710
They were so realistic.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:33.450
Excuse us, we're the stage show actors.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:35.720
We got caught in a speed 
trap on the way here...

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.380
Huh? The show's already over.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:39.830
Huh?

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:44.790
I told you we shouldn't have gone...

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:46.060
Freakin' Leaf Village...

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.540
Ow...

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.830
And so, unbeknownst to everyone,

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:54.500
Lee and his pals saved the 
village from disaster.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:03.460
Thanks to the safety campaign,

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:05.430
accidents are way down,

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.130
and Lady Tsunade couldn't be happier.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:11.020
I was thinking I'd hold a festival,

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:13.270
as a reward for everyone.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.630
A Fall Festival?

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:19.300
I was thinking we'd do it western
style and really cut loose!

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.060
What do you think?

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:27.720
If I detonate this inside the village,
it'll cause mass destruction.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.130
You still want to attack the Leaf?

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.360
Of course!

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.780
I'm going out like this.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:38.020
They might not even take this as a threat.

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:41.440
<b>Leaf Halloween Festival</b>

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:41.440
They're having a Halloween 
festival, apparently.

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:43.890
What's a Halloween?

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:48.700
Well, it's a scary holiday where
witches, monsters, and ghosts...

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.310
...come out to frighten 
people in the night.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:52.540
Frighten them, eh?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.040
More specifically, people 
put on scary costumes,

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:59.150
say "Trick or Treat" and get candy,

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.570
<b>Halloween Party</b>

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:01.090
and rock out at parties.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.800
Sounds pretty weird.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:05.130
It's an American Obon.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.030
An American Obon?

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:10.070
Oh, now I'm definitely in.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:12.560
You are?

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:13.310
<b>Pumpkin</b>

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.810
<b>Pumpkin</b>

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:15.810
I'll sneak my newest masterpiece 
onto the center stage,

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:19.320
and teach them what real 
terror is all about! Hmm!

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.280
I could try to stop him, 
but he won't listen...

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:24.870
Huh?

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:36.210
<b>Deidara's Art is Always a Blast!</b>

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.130
I can't wait to see the looks 
of horror on their faces.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:45.010
Lady Tsunade herself put us in charge
of the Halloween festivities!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.360
Let's all work extra hard!

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.050
Them...

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.800
So they're in charge of the festival?

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.750
What can we do for Halloween?

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.390
I'm not really familiar with it.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.130
Plus we don't have much time.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.650
Well, Halloween is... you know!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:04.570
I know?

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.490
There's um... pumpkins, and stuff.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.750
Pumpkins... They are in season now.

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.470
Then we'll decorate with 
pumpkin jam and soup,

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:15.790
lanterns, roasted squash, citrons...

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:19.320
You idiots! It's not 
the winter solstice.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:23.570
Hey, aren't you the actor from 
the safe driving performance?

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:26.470
No, remember the real ones came later?

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.010
Wait, then who are you?

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.890
I'm, uh—

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.810
I've got it, you're none other than...

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:37.230
a wandering artist, correct?

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.460
Artist...

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:41.680
I see.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.130
He's got strange clothes,

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.660
and his partner had a flair 
for the dramatic, too.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.920
He must be some kind of workaholic,

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.630
that's why he still went 
onstage the other day.

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.780
A workaholic?!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:57.230
Lady Tsunade must want him to
liven up the Halloween festivities.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.830
Y-Yeah, pretty much.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:01.940
You're a lifesaver!

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.610
We're complete newbies!

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.870
Please teach us all about Halloween!

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.510
<i>This took a turn for the weird.</i>

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:15.180
<b>Halloween 
Festival</b>

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.980
<i>But if they don't have 
their little festival,</i>

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:14.560
<i>it'll ruin my plans.</i>

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:19.140
Halloween is a scary holiday where 
witches, monsters, and ghosts...

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.100
...come out to frighten 
people in the night.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.750
I'm still not getting it.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.770
Could you elaborate, please?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.150
Okay...

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:30.110
<i>People put on scary costumes!</i>

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:32.780
First, you'll need scary costumes!

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:34.700
For example:

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.250
You ready?

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.370
Ta-da!

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:42.100
Nothing's scarier than the 
minions of Hell, right?

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.150
I'd say you're just plain adorable.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:46.840
That's not frightening enough, Tenten.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:54.700
People should be shocked into silence
by someone who would entreat with Hell.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.310
What?

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.450
No, no.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:01.060
You've gone so far beyond 
that you look almost holy!

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.810
Mere child’s play, you two.

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.810
This is the face...

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.060
...of true abject terror!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.400
What is...?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.830
A man who's gone far beyond 
just a demon living in Hell.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.810
Nothing can top this.

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:18.490
I have no idea what that could 
mean, but the costumes gr—

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:20.450
Rejected!

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:23.080
You've gone far beyond what 
the censors will allow!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.460
Next is, uh...

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:27.590
<i>Trick or treat!</i>

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.440
Trick or treat!

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:31.670
We go take candy!

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:33.800
I refuse.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:34.470
What?

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.430
Pestering people is no 
better than stealing.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:39.390
The children of this village 
will feel the same way.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:42.410
Don't be such a wet blanket.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:44.600
It's part of the festival!

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:48.520
So we need to create an environment
where candy will be given willingly.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:54.700
Matches! Anyone need matches?

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.790
I can at least warm myself up.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.230
What delicious looking candy!

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.800
Kindly old Granny Guy...

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:19.520
Granny, the yummy candies 
have faded away...

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.850
I think I'm going to, too...

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:26.730
Candy?!

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.640
I'll give you whatever 
you want, take it all!

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:30.960
Let's go with that.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:32.230
Well done.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.150
You approve of this?!

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:38.380
All that's left is to rock 
out at a party, I think...

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.080
Leave everything to me.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:46.280
Well, we've had a lovely evening so far.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:50.460
Now, someone wants to thank 
the founders of the feast!

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:55.020
Dad, Mom...

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.890
Thank you for raising me right.

00:17:57.890 --> 00:18:01.820
I hope I'll be as happy... as you...

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:03.810
Why me?

00:18:04.510 --> 00:18:06.110
This is a great party.

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:09.480
No it's not! No one's rocking out!

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:13.100
We need to let loose 
a bit more, like this.

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.780
I'm not sure that's the problem.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.450
Something tells me this 
isn't very Halloween-y.

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.400
It's very haphazard.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:25.370
It's supposed to be a 
scary night, isn't it?

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:29.580
This isn't scaring me at all.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.170
Are you sure this is right?

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:36.220
You haven't just been saying random
things this whole time, have you?

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.640
Here I am being nice 
and trying to help...

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.550
Do whatever you want!

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:44.470
We can't give up!

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:49.110
If we let our youthful passion explode,
I'm sure something good will come of it!

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:50.150
Explode...

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.320
Did you say explode?

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:54.820
Our young power will 
make a colossal blast.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.230
But what do we do?

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:59.240
There's a clue in there somewhere.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:05.160
Scary costumes, trick or 
treating, rocking out...

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:08.330
The one thing linking them together...

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:11.130
<i>It's an American Obon.</i>

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:13.910
Let's do it!

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:17.130
We'll rock out at a Halloween 
party all night long!

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:22.050
There's not much time, 
do exactly as I say!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.340
We're celebrating the dead,

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:26.060
set up tombstones and polish 
them till they glow!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:30.480
Cows! Horses! We offer up sacrifices!

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.710
<b>Hemp Reeds</b>

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:34.020
Flying Weapons, Needle Storm!

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:36.990
Light a fire to welcome the spirits 
back from the great beyond!

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:44.120
And dance your butts off 
to appease their wrath!

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:46.620
Wait, is this...

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:50.330
What the heck, it's the wrong 
season for the Bon dance!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:54.840
Yes, the Bon dance is a ritual 
done in honor of the dead.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:58.470
If Halloween is like a foreign Obon...

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:00.890
This should be just what we need.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.300
<b>Halloween Party</b>

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:07.310
It's all thanks to you, Mr. Artist.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.480
No, you guys did a good job.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:10.890
Deidara!

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.510
You big goof. How could you 
forget something this important?

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:16.690
Oh, it's your partner...

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:18.610
That's...

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:22.740
I came all this way to bring it to you.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:26.660
Let's finish the job and get outta here!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.240
What's that?

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:40.930
In the end, I guess it's 
my fate to be destroyed.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:45.220
But I won't let you all suffer the same!

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:46.900
D-Deidara?

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:50.850
Farewell.

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.310
What a blast!

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:59.530
Mr. Artist!

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:07.240
It turns out Lady Tsunade didn't 
send for them after all.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:11.750
She just thought up the whole
Halloween idea on the spot.

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:14.550
Then who were they?

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.670
I feel like I've seen 
those outfits before...

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:23.670
We'll meet them again someday.

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:28.840
And so, the evil organization, Akatsuki,
made its presence felt in the Hidden Leaf,

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:32.240
thanks to its members Deidara and Tobi.

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:35.850
They got quite a reward, too.

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.390
Appealing to my emotions...
Well played, Leaf Village.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:44.260
I want a new partner...

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:24.480
Next week is "Steam 
Doesn't Stick to DVDs!"

00:23:21.930 --> 00:23:28.260
<b>Steam Doesn't Stick to DVDs!
October 27th Was Orochimaru's Birthday...</b>

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:28.260
and "October 27th Was 
Orochimaru's Birthday..."

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:29.510
Orochimaru...

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:33.290
His character's really been 
ruined by this anime, huh?

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:35.650
It's the fate of all who 
end up in gag animes.

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:37.980
I feel bad for him, too,
but there's no way around it.

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:39.610
Definitely don't wanna end up like him.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:44.220
I'm sure I'll be fine, but 
you watch yourself, Tobi.

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:47.280
You were pretty ruined by 
the end of this episode.

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:48.720
Just accept it.
